     "text": "{\"count\": 2, \"rationale\": \"crown:obtain is an OR of h3_0:traverse and h3_1:obtain, so both must be cut. h3_1:obtain is an OR of h2_2:traverse and h1_1:access. Both of those come directly from the entry edge1:reach, so h3_1 can only be cut by blocking it or by blocking both of its parents. No single block works: blocking h3_1 leaves h3_0 reachable through h2_2 and h1_1; blocking h3_0 leaves h3_1; blocking h1_1 leaves h2_2, which reaches h3_1; blocking h2_2 leaves h1_1, which reaches h3_1. Blocking {h2_2:traverse, h1_1:access} works, because it cuts h3_1 and the AND step h3_0. So the minimum is 2.\"}"
